Alembic revisions are selected by database alias. Each alias has its own
revision directory and version history.

Configure a migration target in `config.yaml`:

~~~yaml
databases:
  default:
    url: postgresql+asyncpg://...
    runtime_enabled: true
    migration:
      enabled: true
      version_path: migrations/default/versions
      model_modules:
        - apps.models
  market_migration:
    url: postgresql+asyncpg://...
    runtime_enabled: false
    migration:
      enabled: true
      version_path: migrations/market/versions
      model_modules:
        - apps.models.raw
~~~

`runtime_enabled: false` keeps a privileged migration connection out of the
application runtime registry. A read-only runtime alias can use
`read_only: true`; PostgreSQL role permissions remain the final guard.

Run one alias at a time:

~~~text
just migrate default upgrade head
just migrate market_migration upgrade head
just migrate market_migration revision --autogenerate -m "create market tables"
just migrate market_migration downgrade -1
~~~

The alias is required. Unknown aliases and aliases without enabled migration
settings fail before a database connection is opened. The first migration
command creates the configured `version_path`; generated revision files should
be committed to Git.
